course: dictionary
lesson: 15682
title: Tilted: leaning, not straight
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Tilted can be an adjective or a verb. As an adjective, it describes something that leans or slopes, with one side higher than the other. «The picture on the wall was tilted, so I put it straight.» The picture was not level, so tilted means leaning.
explain: Check the clues. A picture that needs straightening must be out of line. Swap in your meaning: «The picture on the wall was leaning» still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: As a verb, tilted is the past form of tilt. «Mia tilted the box, and the pencils rolled out.» She already made the box lean, and the pencils moved because of it.
fact: Tilt means to lean or slope, with one side higher than the other.
fact: «Tilted» is the past form of «tilt»: «She tilted the box.»
fact: «Tilted» as an adjective describes something that is not straight or level.
fact: In science, Earth's axis is tilted about 23 and a half degrees.
fact: That tilt is the reason we have seasons.
exercise: «The picture on the wall was tilted.» What does tilted mean here? | *Leaning, not straight | Shiny and new | Very heavy | Cleaned and painted
exercise: Which word is the past form of tilt? | tilts | tilting | tilter | *tilted
exercise: «Sam tilted his head and asked, "Why?"» What does the tilted head show? | He is asleep | He is angry and shouting | *He is curious and asking a question | He is swimming
test: «The table had one short leg, so it was tilted to one side.» What does tilted to one side mean? | Painted blue | Flat and level | *Leaning, with one side higher | Very, very clean
test: Earth's axis is tilted about 23 and a half degrees. What does this tilt help to cause? | *The seasons | Earthquakes | The sound of thunder | Earth's shape
exam: Which word means leaning or sloping, not straight? | Flat | *Tilted | Level | Straight
